<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francesco Morosini</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1619">1619</a>–<a href="/years/1694">1694</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Francesco Morosini was a Venetian admiral who defended <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heraklion">Candia</a> during the long Ottoman siege before surrendering it in 1669. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morean-war">Morean War</a> he conquered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a> between 1685 and 1687, and during his campaign in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attica">Attica</a> a Venetian shell exploded the Ottoman powder store in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthenon">Parthenon</a>. Elected Doge of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> in 1688, he died on campaign.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/francesco-morosini.jpg" alt="Francesco Morosini" width="320" height="492" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Didier Descouens · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:(Venice)_Portrait_of_doge_Francesco_Morosini_-_Museo_Correr.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
